<!DOCTYPE html><script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/texme@1.2.2"></script>
<textarea>


This document outlines how the __mmdh__ package can be used to
download and preprocess HCES 2023-24 data from the MoSPI microdata
website.

We assume that the `MOSPI_API_KEY` environment variable has been set
prior to running the code in this document.

```{r}
library(mmdh)
## confirm ID no
dlist <- list_datasets()
subset(dlist, grepl("hces", idno, ignore.case = TRUE))
```

The files available for `idno = "DDI-IND-MOSPI-NSS-HCES23-24"` can be
listed using

```{r}
hces202324_files <- list_files("DDI-IND-MOSPI-NSS-HCES23-24")
hces202324_files
```

As we can see, the data are available in several formats. We will use
the SPSS format files.

```{r}
DESTDIR <- "HCES23-24"
ZIPFILE <- file.path(DESTDIR, "HCES_Data_2023-24_SPSS.zip")
if (!dir.exists(DESTDIR)) dir.create(DESTDIR)
download_file(id = "DDI-IND-MOSPI-NSS-HCES23-24",
              base64 = "SENFU19EYXRhXzIwMjMtMjRfU1BTUy56aXA",
              destfile = ZIPFILE)
list.files(DESTDIR)
```
 
Next we unzip the downloaded file.

```{r}
unzip(ZIPFILE, exdir = DESTDIR)
list.files(DESTDIR)
(savfiles <- list.files(file.path(DESTDIR, "HCES_Data_2023-24_SPSS")))
```

Our next task is to read these files, clean them up, remove repeated
columns, and save them in the R binary format. First, we renames these
files.


